title: Building a People's Party
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/placeholder.jpg
view-if: neorevisionism > 0 and peoples_party_support >= 3 and peoples_party = 0 and peoples_party_timer == 0
on-arrival: peoples_party_timer = 6
tags: party_affairs
max-visits: 4
#subtitle: Can the PSOE move beyond the industrial working class?

= Building a People's Party

Contrary to orthodox Marxist predictions, the industrial proletariat is not the whole of Spanish society. The great mass of landless braceros in Andalusia and Extremadura, the persistence of smallholders and shopkeepers, and the growth of a republican urban middle class all confound any simple picture of a working-class majority.

In order to build a <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> majority, many Prietistas and the anti-fascist mobilization current are calling for our party to move beyond the industrial working class, to embrace the braceros, the smallholders, and the urban middle class alongside women of all classes. We can create a new and inclusive vision of the party that encompasses all people who work for a living, which is almost everyone in the country save the landowning oligarchy and top capitalists.

- @support_peoples_party: Yes, we must become a people's party!
- @build_support: We must build additional support before becoming a people's party.
- @support_peoples_party_hard: Despite strong opposition from the Besteirista and Caballerista factions, we will become a people's party.
- @no_new_ideas: No, we will always be a party of the industrial working class.
- @root: Perhaps we can discuss this at a later time.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@build_support
view-if: (neorevisionist_strength + reformist_strength < left_strength + center_strength) or peoples_party_support < 5
on-arrival: peoples_party_support += 1; neorevisionist_strength += 5; left_strength -= 5; left_dissent += 5

Within our party, we are pushing forward proposals for a people's party against the Caballerista left and the Besteiristas.


@support_peoples_party
choose-if: (neorevisionist_strength + reformist_strength >= left_strength + center_strength) and peoples_party_support >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: The opposition is too strong.
on-arrival: neorevisionist_strength += 15; reformist_strength += 15; neorevisionist_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent -= 10; peoples_party = 1; industrial_psoe -= 12; landless_psoe += 10; urban_middle_psoe += 10; smallholder_psoe += 8; catholic_psoe += 8; left_dissent += 25; center_dissent += 20; pce_relation -= 10; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1; ceda_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 5*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent)
achievement: volkspartei

In an emergency conference, we have decided to become a people's party that encompasses all working Spaniards, not just the industrial proletariat and urban poor. The Caballeristas and Besteiristas claim that our new party platform is a betrayal of our founding principles, a turn away from <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span> towards bourgeois opportunism. Whatever the case, we are now a party representing all who labor for a living, not just the factory workers.

Should we run a new campaign to publicize our new platform?

- @campaign_workers
- @campaign_middle
- @campaign_rural
- @campaign_unemployed
- @campaign_women



@support_peoples_party_hard
subtitle: This will increase dissent.
view-if: (neorevisionist_strength + reformist_strength < left_strength + center_strength) or (peoples_party_support < 4)
on-arrival: neorevisionist_strength += 10; reformist_strength += 8; peoples_party = 1; industrial_psoe -= 15; landless_psoe += 10; urban_middle_psoe += 10; smallholder_psoe += 8; catholic_psoe += 8; left_dissent += 40; center_dissent += 40; pce_relation -= 10; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1; ceda_relation += 4*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 4*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent)
achievement: volkspartei

It is an arduous and contentious process, but we have pushed through the proposal to become a people's party. The Caballeristas and Besteiristas claim that our new party platform is a betrayal of our founding principles, a turn away from <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span> towards bourgeois opportunism. Whatever the case, we are now a party representing all who labor for a living, not just the factory workers.

Should we run a new campaign to publicize our new platform?

- @campaign_workers
- @campaign_middle
- @campaign_rural
- @campaign_unemployed
- @campaign_women
- @campaign_catholics

@campaign_workers
title: Campaign among the industrial workers, to assuage their doubts about our changes.
on-arrival: industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent);

The industrial workers are still a key part of our constituency, and we must not alienate them in the transformation of our party.

@campaign_middle
title: Campaign among the middle classes.
on-arrival: smallholder_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 6*(1-dissent)

As a people's party, we represent the professionals and small businesspeople of the middle class, and they are becoming receptive to our messages.

@campaign_rural
title: Campaign among the braceros.
choose-if: rural_policy > 0
unavailable-subtitle: We have not enacted any rural policies yet.
on-arrival: landless_psoe += 7*(1-dissent)

As a people's party, we represent the landless braceros of the great estates as well, and they are becoming receptive to our messages.

@campaign_unemployed
title: Campaign among the unemployed.
on-arrival: unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent);

As a people's party, the urban poor are still a key part of our constituency.

@campaign_women
title: Campaign among women of all classes.
on-arrival: industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent);

As a people's party, we represent women of all classes, though we have not yet extended them the vote on equal terms within our own ranks of thought.

@campaign_catholics
title: Campaign among political Catholics.
on-arrival: catholic_psoe += 7*(1-dissent);

Catholics have historically been tied to the <span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span>, but there is no reason why our party cannot appeal to the devout working poor among them.


@no_new_ideas
on-arrival: neorevisionist_strength -= 6; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; center_strength += 8; left_strength += 3; peoples_party = 0; peoples_party_support -= 3

The <span style="color: #c00000;">Socialists</span> have been and will always be a party of the industrial working class.
